{{Quote|The Emperor's wayfinder is in the Imperial vault. At delta 3-6, transient 9-3-6, bearing 3-2&hellip;on a moon in the Endor system.|[[C-3PO]]|<ref name="TROS Date">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']] to one [[Standard year|year]] after the events of [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]. As ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of ''The Force Awakens'' to [[34 ABY]], the events of ''The Rise of Skywalker'' must occur in [[35 ABY]].</ref>}}
'''Kef Bir''', designated '''IX3244-C''' and known as the '''Ocean Moon of Endor''', was an [[ocean]] [[moon]] [[orbit]]ing the [[gas giant]] [[Endor (planet)|Endor]] in the [[Endor system]].<ref name="TROSVD" /> [[Jannah]], a [[human]] [[Gender|female]] and freedom fighter who (by the [[time]] of the [[First Order-Resistance War]]) had led a [[Company 77|tribe]] of brave and noble [[Soldier|warriors]],<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> lived on the moon after the tribe mutinied at the [[Battle of Ansett Island]]. Some of the debris and wreckage of the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|second Death Star]] fell onto Kef Bir.<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Description==
An ocean moon, Kef Bir orbited the planet Endor, in the Endor system of [[Outer Rim Territories]]' [[Moddell sector]],<ref name="TROSVD" /> positioned at the coordinates H-16<ref name="Beginner Game" /> on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="Rebel Dossier">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: Rebel Dossier]]''</ref> The moon used to be almost entirely underwater, until several cataclysmic events had vented the water into the atmosphere and caused tectonic upheaval, that revealed more and more landmasses.<ref name="TROSEE">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition]]''</ref> Since then it was primarily covered by oceans, such as the [[Kef Sur Ocean]], and [[grass]]land islands, such as the [[Angkuadi islands]]. The moon had at least one continent, called [[Shoduah continent|Shoduah]]. At high tide, the waves could reach a height of over 120 meters. It had a saline environment.<ref name="TROSVD" />

==History==
At some point in its history, the moon was named Kef Bir by the [[Ewok]]s of the adjacent [[Endor|Forest Moon of Endor]].<ref name="TROSVD" />

The Death Star II was, originally, planned to orbit Kef Bir. However, as the moon had few ores, it was relocated to the forest moon with no garrison stationed on Kef Bir.<ref name="TROSVD" />

In [[4 ABY]], a successful attack by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] on the Death Star II ended in its destruction. The resulting debris, including what was left of the [[superlaser]] dish and the Emperor's Throne Room, fell into Kef Bir's orbit and eventually crashed into its seas. The explosion of the reactor lead to abnormal physics, and several massive pieces of debris were launched into [[hyperspace]]. No scientist nor sentient being had witnessed the event, nor could anyone explain what variables prevented a catastrophe.<ref name="TROSVD" /> Wreckage from the moon-sized base had not only rained-down for years onto Kef Bir but had collided with several nearby [[asteroid]]s, creating a chain-reaction of [[bolide]] hits to the moon's surface and atmosphere.<ref name="TROSEE" /> After the Death Star crashed, toxic leakage and nuclear waste from the base poisoned the marine ecosystems on Kef Bir, fueling a global ecological catastrophe.<ref name="TROSVD" />

Decades before [[35 ABY]],<ref name="TROS Date" /> Kef Bir had experienced several cataclysmic events which had vented the moon’s water into the atmosphere and caused further tectonic upheaval, creating more, and new, landmasses. Some theorized that the destruction of the second Death Star was to blame.<ref name="TROSEE" /> In the decade before 35 ABY,<ref name="TROS Date" /> the moon’s geologic processes had calmed down, and life was finding a hold.<ref name="TROSEE" />

[[File:KefBir-SWcom.png|thumb|left|250px|The wreckage of the second Death Star lay in Kef Bir's sea.]]
In 35 ABY,<ref name="TROS Date" /> [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], [[Finn]], [[Poe Dameron]], and [[Chewbacca]] arrived on Kef Bir following directions found on [[Blade of Ochi of Bestoon|Ochi's dagger]] and translated by [[C-3PO]], to secure a [[Wayfinder]] to [[Exegol]] belonging to [[Darth Sidious]] aboard the wreckage of Death Star II. There, they met [[Jannah]], a former [[First Order stormtrooper|First Order Stormtrooper]] who resided on the ocean moon, along with her [[Company 77|tribe]]. Rey found the Wayfinder in the Emperor's Throne Room, but was confronted by [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]], who destroyed it. The two dueled, with Rey stabbing Ren as he was distracted, sensing the [[death]] of his mother, [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]]. Rey [[Force healing|healed]] him and took his [[TIE/wi modified interceptor]], leaving him stranded aboard the Death Star II's wreckage.<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Behind the scenes==
Kef Bir first appeared in the [[2019]] [[sequel trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']].<ref name="Episode IX" /> Footage was recorded in Buckinghamshire, England, and then digitally transformed into the stormy coast seen in the movie.<ref name="TROSVD" />

[[File:Star_Tours_Kef_Bir_concept_art.jpg|Concept art of Star Tours' Kef Bir scene|thumb|right|250px]]
On [[October 23]], 2019, the Disney Parks Blog announced that the ''[[Star Tours: The Adventures Continue]]'' rides at [[Disneyland]], [[Disney's Hollywood Studios]], [[Disneyland Paris]], and [[Tokyo Disneyland]] would be updated to include a scene set on Kef Bir, similar to previous updates that added planets featured in [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''The Force Awakens'']] and [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''The Last Jedi'']].<ref name="DPB">{{DPB|url=2019/10/here-we-go-again-exciting-updates-to-star-tours-the-adventures-continue|text='Here We Go Again!' Exciting Updates to Star Tours &mdash; The Adventures Continue}}</ref>

